--- !u!114 &779198843244269177
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4552455287794273465}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UnityEngine.UI::UnityEngine.UI.Text
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 23
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "START A SESSION\nOpen Scenarios (F2), choose a JSON scenario, select Load
    selected, then Start training.\n\nMOVE & INTERACT\nWASD: move. Mouse: look. Aim
    at equipment within reach and press E. Esc closes a panel. Enter or C continues
    a message when no panel is open.\n\nFIVE CLINICAL HOTSPOTS\nPatient / bed: assessment.
    Monitor: current vitals and trends. Ventilator: scenario intervention. EHR Terminal:
    patient record and documentation. Call Button: escalation. Available actions
    are listed in the training panel.\n\nDOCUMENT AN INTERVENTION\n1. Open the EHR
    Terminal.\n2. Read the patient context, vitals and missing requirements.\n3.
    Select the required form tab.\n4. Enter the fields marked *.\n5. Choose Save
    / Submit on EACH required form.\n6. Check the Saved status and completion feedback.\n\nERRORS
    & TIMING\nAn empty required field keeps the documentation gate blocked. Fill
    the highlighted requirement and save again. Typing without saving does not pass
    the gate. A decision countdown can change the scenario if it expires. Alarms
    use text and colour as well as sound.\n\nREVIEW & EXPORT\nAt completion, review
    your score, decision path and saved or missing documentation. Export JSON saves
    the full session log locally. Copy path copies the saved file location.\n\nREPEAT
    TRAINING\nScenarios \u2192 Reset scenario \u2192 Confirm reset clears the current
    run and EHR documentation. Export first if you want to retain your log, then
    select Start training.\n\nTRAINING SCOPE\nThis desktop 3D simulation uses fictional
    data. Score rewards and penalties are scenario rules, not clinical validation.
    No VR headset is required."
